  "policy_sha256": "84f656b16099dcb248866f714453e5bd3e275bdb5d4929c4fad838ee8b29ed2c",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "gv-742577-b00001",
      "text": "Armenia and Azerbaijan exchanged fire on July 28, resulting in the deadliest clash since a Russia-brokered ceasefire ended the 44-day war between Armenia and Azerbaijan in November 2020. The two countries blamed each other for starting the shoot-out and violating the November ceasefire agreement.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 297,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.azadliq.org/a/azerbaycan-ermenistan-doyush-yarali-itki/31380710.html",
        "https://www.azatutyun.am/a/31380642.html",
        "https://www.rferl.org/a/azerbaijan-armenia-border-clashes/31381068.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-742577-b00002",
      "text": "According to Azerbaijan's Ministry of Defense, at least two Azerbaijanian servicemen were wounded. While the Armenian Defense Ministry said three Armenian servicemen were killed and four wounded. The most recent clashes come just days after the two countries traded fire near the Armenian village of Yeraskh and the Azerbaijani village of Heydarabad.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 299,
      "body_end": 649,
      "source_links": [
        "https://globalvoices.org/2021/07/26/fresh-clashes-on-nakhchivan-border/?preview_id=741718&preview_nonce=66e1c95336&_thumbnail_id=741779&preview=true",
        "https://mod.gov.az/en/news/the-azerbaijan-army-positions-in-the-kalbajar-region-were-once-again-subjected-to-fire-36924.html",
        "https://www.azatutyun.am/a/31380642.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-742577-b00003",
      "text": "Leyla Abdullayeva, spokesperson for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in Azerbaijan said in a tweet that Armenia bore the responsibility for recent clashes:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 651,
      "body_end": 805,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-742577-b00004",
      "text": "Meanwhile, Armenia's Ministry of Defense said, “All responsibility for the aggravation of the situation lies with the military-political leadership of Azerbaijan.” While the country's Ministry of Foreign Affairs said in a statement that “the Azerbaijani side has been deliberately initiating escalation.”",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 807,
      "body_end": 1111,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.mfa.am/en/interviews-articles-and-comments/2021/07/28/mfa_statement/11012"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-742577-b00005",
      "text": "Later that day, both sides agreed to deescalate tensions in a move proposed by Russia.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 1113,
      "body_end": 1199,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-742577-b00006",
      "text": "Earlier in July, both the EU and the US urged the two sides to reduce tensions.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 1201,
      "body_end": 1280,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-742577-b00007",
      "text": "Last year's war claimed at least 6,900 lives. The ceasefire signed in November saw Azerbaijan regain control over all seven adjacent districts and parts of Nagorno-Karabakh previously controlled by ethnic Armenians.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 1282,
      "body_end": 1497,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.rferl.org/a/azerbaijan-armenia-border-clashes/31381068.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    }
  ],
